# Skin fidelity

- Main window is 275×116 skin pixels. EQ is 275×116. Playlist steps are 25 px horizontal and 29 px vertical from that minimum. Shade on main and EQ is 14 px.
- Scale factors are 1, 2, and 4, nearest-neighbor. Double-size doubles skin pixels, then the display factor multiplies. Fractional OS scales letterbox. Bilinear skin chrome is a bug.
- `main.bmp` that is not 275×116 fails the skin. Do not scale it to fit.
- Shells consume the core atlas. They do not parse BMP.
- Bitmap font for classic chrome only. Library, lyrics, and any playlist row with a missing glyph use platform text in `pledit.txt` colors.
- Sprite coordinates that are not fixture-locked do not get invented. See `docs/spec/skin-format.md`.
